plicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUOKA HIDEHITO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MITA SHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SANTEN PHARMA CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUOKA, HIDEHITO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITA, SHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SANTEN PHARMACEUTICAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUOKA HIDEHITO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MITA SHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUOKA, HIDEHITO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITA, SHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A newly found pharmacological effect of a cysteine derivative of strongly inhibiting angiogenesis. Owing to this effect, this cysteine derivative is expected as being useful as a remedy for diseases in which angiogenesis participates, in particular, retinal diseases such as diabetic retinitis, macular degeneration, retinal venous obliteration and retinal arterial obliteration, angiogenic glaucoma and tumors such as angioma.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>On a découvert récemment un nouvel effet pharmacologique d'un dérivé de la cystéine qui s'avère un puissant inhibiteur de l'angiogenèse. En raison de cet effet, ce dérivé devrait pouvoir servir de remède aux maladies liées à l'angiogenèse, et en particulier aux lésions de la rétine, telles que la rétinite diabétique, la dégénérescence maculaire, l'oblitération de l'artère rétinienne, le glaucome angiogène, et les tumeurs du type angiome.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>